ozz-raw-track-interpolation: refuse a raw track keyframe's unknown mode

A raw track's keyframe stores its interpolation as one byte, and Load cast
whatever byte the archive held to RawTrackInterpolation::Value: a value
that is neither kStep nor kLinear, which is undefined to load back out, and
which TrackBuilder then tests to build the track's step bits.

Load refuses a mode past kLinear through the archive's refusal record.

Evidence: zozz's src/integration_test.zig loads a raw track of each value
type whose keyframe holds mode 2, and upstream loads it; zozz's fuzz
property, building such a track under UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, stopped
in TrackBuilder::Build with "load of value 130, which is not valid for type
'RawTrackInterpolation::Value'" (both measured, 2026-10-31).

diff --git a/libs/ozz/src/animation/offline/raw_track.cc b/libs/ozz/src/animation/offline/raw_track.cc
index 3059eb6..d60c6d6 100644
--- a/libs/ozz/src/animation/offline/raw_track.cc
+++ b/libs/ozz/src/animation/offline/raw_track.cc
@@ -66,6 +66,11 @@ struct Extern<animation::offline::RawTrackKeyframe<_ValueType>> {
           _keyframes[i];
       uint8_t interp;
       _archive >> interp;
+      if (interp > animation::offline::RawTrackInterpolation::kLinear) {
+        _archive.Refuse("RawTrackKeyframe.interpolation", interp,
+                        animation::offline::RawTrackInterpolation::kLinear);
+        return;
+      }
       keyframe.interpolation =
           static_cast<animation::offline::RawTrackInterpolation::Value>(interp);
       _archive >> keyframe.ratio;
